Draw a surface its opaque region covers without its alpha (Omarchy Mobile)

A client's opaque region says its content is opaque there, but Hyprland
drew such a surface with the alpha of its buffer. Chromium (Qt WebEngine)
leaves an opaque page's alpha at 0 in a buffer that has an alpha channel:
on screen nothing shows (nothing is drawn below an opaque surface and the
output has no alpha), but every picture of the window, a toplevel capture
for an app switcher's card or a screenshot, was transparent where the page
was. A surface whose opaque region covers it is drawn as RGBX instead.

--- a/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
+++ b/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
@@ -1308,6 +1308,17 @@
     const auto surface                       = g_pHyprRenderer->m_renderData.surface;
     const auto WORK_BUFFER_IMAGE_DESCRIPTION = g_pHyprRenderer->m_renderData.pMonitor->workBufferImageDescription();
 
+    // A surface whose opaque region covers it is drawn without its alpha: the
+    // client says it is opaque there. Chromium leaves an opaque page's alpha
+    // at 0 in a buffer that has one; drawn with it, pictures of the window (a
+    // toplevel capture, a screenshot) were transparent where the page was.
+    if ((shaderFeatures & SH_FEAT_RGBA) && surface.valid() && !surface->m_current.opaque.empty()) {
+        CRegion uncovered{CBox{{}, surface->m_current.size}};
+        uncovered.subtract(surface->m_current.opaque);
+        if (uncovered.empty())
+            shaderFeatures &= ~SH_FEAT_RGBA;
+    }
+
     // chosenSdrEotf contains the valid eotf for this display
 
     const auto SOURCE_IMAGE_DESCRIPTION = [&] {
